The code seems fine, and the array list is tested well on an integer. But if the array list consists of objects, the contract test code doesn't work. What could have caused this bug?

To reproduce the bug, you should provide a few arrays of objects along with a few arbitrary elements. 

For instance, use something like this:

@PexMethod 
public void TestMethod3( [PexAssumeUnderTest] MyClass[] arr) 
{ 
    AssumePrecondition.IsTrue(true); // to run the test 
    arr[2] = arr[3]; // to generate different paths 
    arr[1] = arr[3]; // to generate different paths 
}

In this case, my test class looks like this:

namespace PexStressTest
